claim.claim-text:
an elongated handle;
a guide face attached to the elongated handle, the guide face being of a shape configured to engage an articular surface of the distal radius bone;
the guide face comprising first, second, and third visual cues (502, 504, 506);
the first visual cue (502) adapted to substantially align with a palmar corner of a radioulnar joint located on the distal radius;
the second visual cue (504) adapted to substantially align with a dorsal corner of a radioulnar joint located on the distal radius;
the third visual cue (506) adapted to substantially align with a tip of a radial styloid located on the distal radius;
the guide face further comprising an opening (508) designating the insertion point, the opening placed at a location on the guide face relative to the visual cues (502, 504, 506); and
the opening (508) being adapted to mark a spot for the insertion point on the articular surface of the distal radius bone.
